/-
Support definitions and elementary lemmas for
`Work.SSGRoute.local_tate_duality_archimedean`.

The archimedean (real place) case of local Tate duality is the pairing

  `H¹(⟨c⟩, E) × H¹(⟨c⟩, DualMod p (E ⊗ T)) → 𝔽_p`

where `c` is the complex conjugation (an involution) and `⟨c⟩ ≅ ℤ/2`.  This file provides

* a choice of generator `t0` of a rank-one `𝔽_p`-module `T` with its coordinate functional
  `coord` (`coord t0 = 1`, `coord t • t0 = t`),
* the associated linear maps `toE : E ⊗ T →ₗ E` and `tensorLift : (E →ₗ 𝔽_p) → (E ⊗ T →ₗ 𝔽_p)`,
* the pairing `Ach.archPair` (the `if p = 2 then ... else 0` formula of the proof),
* the elementary reduction of the cocycle/coboundary conditions on a cyclic group of order
  two generated by `c` to conditions at `c`,
* characteristic-two arithmetic in `ZMod p` for `p = 2`,
* the double-annihilator fact `mem_range_iff_forall_dual`.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.SSGRoute.Interfaces
import Submission.Work.SSGRoute.DualMod.Main
